WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:33.710
Mr. Penguin's Hobbies!

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.510
Mr. Penguin,

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.910
why are you so smirky today?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.110
Couldn't you just say "smiley"?

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.380
What happened?

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.700
Well, you see...

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.370
I'm going to be opening 
my own exhibit.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.340
Exhibit <i>(koten)</i>?

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.710
Coffee 
Dictionary

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.050
That would be a dictionary <i>(jiten)</i>.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.700
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.720
That would be a traditional 
short coat (hanten).

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.800
That would be a somersault <i>(zenten)</i>.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.040
I said an exhibit. An ex-hib-it!

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.380
Wow, that's amazing.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.020
What do you do at an exhibit?

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.030
You'll just have to come and see.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.280
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.930
Where is it at?

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.790
It should be right around here.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:34.920
I think it's right there.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:41.890
Penguin Art Exhibit
~Penguin  The New Age  New World~

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.890
Penguin Art Exhibit.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.320
Penguin: The New Age, New World.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.900
I think he set the bar too high.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.790
What does that mean?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.860
I think you'll understand 
once we go inside.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.390
Hello!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.320
Pardon the intrusion.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.030
Well, hello. Welcome.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.120
Mr. Penguin.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:04.870
What?

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.970
Mr. Penguin,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.930
you certainly like to look the part.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:16.820
To Mr. Penguin 
from Penguin

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.000
Who cares?!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.700
Come, look at my paintings!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.210
First, look at this piece.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.830
With this,

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.300
I was trying to express 
a flower's life force

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.270
as it soaks in the sun's 
rays and blossoms.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.030
It's titled...

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.540
"Dandelions"!

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.650
I'm pretty sure I've 
seen this before...

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.320
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.700
What is it?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.500
You have such sloping 
shoulders, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:45.570
What of it?

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.800
How do you carry a bag?

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.080
Would you look at the 
paintings, Panda?

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.870
Next, take a look at this piece.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.100
In this piece, I'd like people to appreciate

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.690
the familiar yet dissociative feeling 
of real-life objects set in a painting.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.260
It's titled...

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.470
"The White Egg of the Pyrenees."

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.180
I'm pretty sure I've 
seen this before...

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.880
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.760
What is it?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.640
Where exactly are your 
eyes, Mr. Penguin?

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.120
Right here.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.150
Would you just look over here?

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.600
What a pretty wall!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.980
I'm asking you to look 
at the painting!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.630
So this is the next piece.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.360
This is a piece that expresses 
in detail the uneasiness

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.610
and pathology of the people 
living in modern society.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.170
It's titled...

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.130
"The Yawn"?

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.670
How did you know?

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:48.860
Just had a feeling.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.440
What's this?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.860
These are paintings of seas.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:04:59.780
This one is the Baltic Sea.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.920
This is the Bering Sea.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.570
And this one is the Arctic Sea.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.030
You see, I had a hard time 
successfully expressing

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.510
the water temperature in 
the Bering Sea painting.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.190
Wow, that's amazing.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.210
So, where are the paintings?

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.000
What?!

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.050
I'm guessing this is from your 
blue period, Mr. Penguin.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.060
Thanks for the vague follow 
through, Polar Bear.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.180
So, how was it?

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.010
Let me know what you think.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:35.820
Hmm... I think it lacked originality.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:36.450
What?

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:37.630
How do you mean?

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.370
In general.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.760
Why?!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.610
Hurry and show me your 
paintings, Mr. Penguin!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.880
You know,

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.410
it's perfectly fine if 
you don't say anything.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.460
Look! I got a customer!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.710
I'm sure he's someone that 
understands art, unlike you two!

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.270
Pardon the intrusion.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:14.940
He left.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.060
Mr. Penguin, I really like this.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.650
What? Which painting?

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.720
This carpet is really 
comfortable to sleep on.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:24.760
That's what you're talking about?!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.660
Or rather, would you not sleep there!

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.420
Would you like to sleep, 
too, Mr. Penguin?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.610
No!

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:40.830
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.140
I think it'd be best for you

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.190
to find some hobbies other than

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.540
sleeping and eating, Panda.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.640
I have some.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.340
Like what?

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.680
I like to lay around.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.260
I don't think that counts as a hobby.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.210
You seem to have a lot 
of hobbies, Polar Bear.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.160
Well, there's surfing 
and scuba diving.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.610
In the winter, I like 
to snowboard and ski.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.770
I also like mountain climbing.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.580
Wow. I think I'll do that, too.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:10.030
I don't think I can picture you 
doing any of those, Panda.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.080
Grizzly loves to ride motorcycles.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.490
He loves to go touring on his days off.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.480
That's right. He has 
pictures around his bar.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.140
How cool!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.070
I'll do that, too.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.600
Can you even ride a motorcycle?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.510
I doubt you'd be able to get your license.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.870
If I recall correctly,

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.630
Mr. Llama's 
hobby is bonsai.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:33.670
Bonsai?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.310
What do you think about 
these branches?

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:39.640
Oh, I should prune them.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.950
It's a little prickly.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.030
So he's eating them.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.880
He's combining practicality 
with his hobby.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:53.550
I'll do that, too.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:56.280
Everything sounds appealing to you.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.790
Sloth says he likes knitting.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.520
Winter

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:05.480
Spring

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:08.530
Summer

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.530
Fall

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:16.240
Winter

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:16.260
I hear he's been knitting 
a scarf for three years.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.700
Hopefully he'll be able to 
use it while he's alive.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.440
I wonder why he even started.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.280
I'll do that, too.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.050
I think you just want to 
say that phrase now.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.850
And Mr. Tortoise's hobby...

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.450
I thought he liked cameras.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:35.120
Nope. Apparently he 
started playing squash.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.200
Squash?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.090
You know...

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.940
That sounds more like the 
other person's hobby,

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.460
rather than Tortoise's...

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.930
I'll do that, too.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.820
Do you want to draw, Panda?

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.660
I wouldn't mind teaching you.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.300
I'd rather not.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.430
Apparently not, Mr. Penguin.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.940
Why don't you two go home?

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.290
What are your hobbies, Mr. Penguin?

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.720
Are you really asking me that here?

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:18.880
I wonder if this is the place.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:19.870
I think so.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.830
Look! I'm sure Miss Penko and 
the others understand art.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.230
You two, just watch!

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.410
Which ones are the paintings?

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:28.500
This one?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.650
That's a wall.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:30.660
What about this?

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.240
That's just a wall, too.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.550
I think it's over here.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:35.560
I agree.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.220
Where are the paintings?

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.550
This is just another wall.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.140
There are only walls.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.290
I'm tired.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.490
I'm starving.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.220
Let's go eat.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:45.290
Yes.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.770
They're so rude.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.860
The wall's right here.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.190
Thanks for the follow, Panda.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.780
But that's a painting.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.330
Mr. Penguin,

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.370
I brought a gift.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.290
Wow! They look delicious!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.340
It's delicious.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.010
I'm sure Miss Penko and the others 
will understand someday...

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.260
Polar Bear...

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.590
In about fifty years.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.630
I wonder if I'll be alive.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:43.990
Polar Bear's Café

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:48.870
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.300
Their Childhood Days.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.930
Hello.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.600
Welcome.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.190
Welcome!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.430
Oh?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:09.670
Mr. Llama?!

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:14.300
Are you all right?

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:14.940
Yes.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:17.090
Sorry about that.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:19.310
Didn't mean to scare ya.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:20.500
Not at all.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:23.940
I apologize for losing my composure.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.490
The entrance's light went out,

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.160
so I asked Grizzly to come over.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.630
I came because you said you 
had an urgent matter.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.810
Why the hell am I here just 
to change a light bulb?

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.130
You can do that yourself.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.520
Sorry for troubling you.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.710
As long as you acknowledge that.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:45.610
Oh, now that I think of it,

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:49.000
the rain gutter by the 
terrace needs work.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.270
Could you fix that, too?

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.470
Why you...

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.550
Just who do you think I am?!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.980
My friend.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:08.280
Mr. Grizzly is such a nice guy.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:09.660
Though his face is scary.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.500
But he's so cool.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.110
Though his face is scary.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:15.910
Sorry it's scary.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.380
I fixed it.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.210
The next time it rains,

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:24.240
let me know how it holds up.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:25.330
Got it.

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:26.300
Also...

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:29.360
Damn it, would you stop it?!

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:30.450
Coffee!

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:32.020
Black, right?

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:33.310
Yeah.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:39.870
Hey, how long have you 
two been friends?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.030
I wonder how long it's been...

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.490
You forgot?

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:47.160
For a long time.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.150
Wow.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.960
I'm the king of Alaska!

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:12.810
How was that?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.520
Whatcha doin'?

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.520
Who are you?

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.440
I'm Polar Bear.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.530
Polar Bear?

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:06.320
Fear me! Run away!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.750
I'm Grizzly! I'm special! I'm a king!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.160
A king <i>(ouja)</i>?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.610
That's porridge <i>(ojiya)</i>.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.280
That's a temple <i>(jinja)</i>.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.880
That's a sage <i>(kenja)</i>.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.200
That's a ninja!

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.300
That's a billionaire <i>(okumanchouja)</i>.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.040
You're not scared at all, are you?!

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:31.790
Nope.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.660
When grizzlies grow up,

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.980
truly become the kings of Alaska!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.940
When polar bears grow up...

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.970
They become the world's 
largest land carnivore.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.850
Damn it! I'm done with 
the king game! Done!

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:55.870
Grizzly!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.440
Who do you think you are?

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.040
I'm Polar Bear!

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:05.360
You told me that yesterday!

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.130
What are you doing here?

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.010
Do you wanna play?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.010
What? Why would I play with yo—

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.310
I'm not playing the king game anymore!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.220
Really?

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.440
Then let's play something else.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.990
How was that?!

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.290
I won the race!

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:48.470
Well, my stuff is heavier.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.450
Is that bag that heavy?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.220
Yup.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.760
Here, hold it.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:01.030
Why do I have to hold it?

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.110
Huh?

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.150
Ready, go!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.920
Hey! No fair!

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:16.120
Hey! Wait!

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:26.080
Where the heck did he go?

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.330
Grizzly.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:31.630
Over here.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.590
I'll introduce you two.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.830
This is my older brother.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.260
Don't we look alike?

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.480
I see...

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:43.810
Oh, nice to meet you, sir.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.920
My name is Grizzly.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.050
He's just a dog!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:17:03.710
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.610
You know,

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.060
you're pretty different.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.170
Really?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.980
Everyone else that sees me 
gets scared and runs away.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.140
But you haven't.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.100
Scary?

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:21.990
Jeez.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:26.060
Talking to you puts me off balance.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.420
Why?

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:30.200
I don't know!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.200
Delicious!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:42.200
There are so many delicious 
things to eat in the fall!

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:45.350
Well, they do call autumn the 
"season of good appetite."

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.670
What do you usually eat, Grizzly?

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.420
Well, I eat fish, too.

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:54.630
But the best thing to eat 
in autumn is berries.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:56.560
I see.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.840
What do you eat, Polar Bear?

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:00.800
Seals.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.700
Sometimes walruses.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:05.230
I even eat whale.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:08.060
Th-That's huge...

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.770
Do you always catch things that big?

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:12.190
About once a week.

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:14.640
Most of the time, 
I don't catch anything.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.740
What do you do on days that 
you can't catch anything?

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.630
I laze around.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:23.200
I don't know if I should 
be impressed or what...

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.040
Well, all I can do is wait.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.710
I'm...

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.340
a bit hungry.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.630
Y-You can't eat me!

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:42.650
I'm home.

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:44.100
Thank you for having me.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.460
No one else is home, though.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.700
My mom won't be home until later.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:51.810
I see.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.050
Then I'll make us something to eat.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.570
What can you make?

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.710
Well...

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.540
There's bear paw stew.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:09.450
Just kidding.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:13.210
Your jokes are scary!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.170
There's salmon.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:20.130
I love salmon stew <i>(shichuu)</i>.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.270
Space <i>(uchuu)</i>?

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.260
No.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:26.930
Underground <i>(chichuu)</i>?

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:29.100
No.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:30.970
Bugs <i>(konchuu)</i>?

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:32.430
Light pole <i>(denchuu)</i>?

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:34.820
I said stew!

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.470
You're so short-tempered.

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.370
Whose fault is that?

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.340
Let's eat!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.100
How is it?

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:15.090
It's delicious!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.110
I'm home.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.410
Sorry I got back so late.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:34.960
Oh?

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.660
Well, aren't they precious.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.790
Thanks for the food...

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:08.160
So you two have been friends 
since you were little.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.610
So you're what they call 
"childhood friends."

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:13.710
Well, we have been together 
since we were kids.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:17.170
You can say we're sort of 
stuck with each other.

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:25.050
I'm hungry.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.140
Well, it is the evening.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:30.160
Guess that story ran a little long.

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.590
I'm gonna head home.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:35.350
Oh, wait a sec.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.030
What?

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.830
It smells so good!

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.130
Wow.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:49.910
What's that?

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.490
You made salmon stew.

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:58.120
You liked it, right?

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:01.680
You...

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:05.200
Come on, have some.

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:10.540
Let's eat!

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:14.350
It's so good!

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:15.980
It really is.

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:16.810
Yes.

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.960
You're good at cooking, if nothing else.

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:22.000
I'm good at cooking, as well, you mean.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:25.160
Next Time

00:23:58.170 --> 00:23:59.760
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:00.960
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.370
Next week's Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:02.960
Too early!

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:03.630
I'll wait.

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:04.340
Good.

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:06.820
Mr. Penguin, if you were reincarnated,

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:08.500
whose subordinate would you be?

00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:09.840
I don't think I'd like 
to be a subordinate.

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:12.290
If you were reincarnated, 
what hardships would you face?

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:13.460
I'd rather not face any.

00:24:13.460 --> 00:24:15.040
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:17.640
This is your part, Polar Bear!

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:18.280
Sorry.

00:24:18.280 --> 00:24:19.460
Concentrate.

00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:21.100
Next week's Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:21.890
will explode!

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:22.750
It will not.

00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:24.000
The New Panda
Reunion at the Grizzly Bar

00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:24.000
Enjoy!
